```apex
/**
 * Synchronously closes forgotten open Opportunities whose CloseDate is strictly
 * before the given cutoff (an Opportunity closing on the cutoff date stays open).
 *
 * Invoked directly by a nightly Schedulable. Uses the list-form SOQL for-loop so
 * the QueryLocator yields 200-record chunks; each chunk is updated and then
 * dropped from heap. We never hold the full result set in memory.
 *
 * What I would change, and why:
 * 1. Promote this to Database.Batchable if volume can grow. Synchronous Apex
 *    allows 10,000 DML rows and 150 DML statements; Opportunity triggers on
 *    every chunk multiply SOQL/DML/CPU. Batch Apex (scope 200) is the durable
 *    pattern for a nightly close job.
 * 2. Use Database.update(chunk, false) and log SaveResult errors. A single
 *    allOrNone update means one validation-rule failure rolls back every close
 *    from that night, which is brittle for a scheduled job.
 * 3. without sharing so the job can close records the scheduling user cannot see.
 */
public without sharing class StaleOpportunityCloser {
    public static Integer closeStale(Date cutoff) {
        if (cutoff == null) {
            return 0;
        }

        Integer closedCount = 0;

        for (List<Opportunity> chunk : [
            SELECT Id
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE IsClosed = false
            AND CloseDate < :cutoff
        ]) {
            for (Opportunity opp : chunk) {
                opp.StageName = 'Closed Lost';
            }
            update chunk;
            closedCount += chunk.size();
        }

        return closedCount;
    }
}
